{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016hfWiYtFk3rEu2MdDckUr3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Agent assembly: provider wiring, the output union, the rendering gate, budgets.\n2\t\n3\tWhat this module is responsible for, and nothing else:\n4\t\n5\t- **Provider wiring.** The local POC defaults to the token-backed Claude Code\n6\t  subscription account; the Anthropic SDK remains an explicit, potentially\n7\t  metered transport. SDK retries are 0 —\n8\t  `harness.retry` is the single retry owner (ADR-003).\n9\t- **The output union.** The model chooses between `AnswerDraft`,\n10\t  `ClarificationNeeded` and `Unsupported`; `ask()` widens that to\n11\t  `HarnessOutput` by attaching the preserved envelope fields and by adding the\n12\t  `BudgetExceeded` branch the model can never select (architecture §5).\n13\t- **The rendering gate.** An output validator applies `harness.rendering` and\n14\t  hands violations back as `ModelRetry`, so a run self-corrects rather than\n15\t  returning something the eval suite would fail later.\n16\t- **The control envelope.** `UsageLimits` for steps and tool calls, one wall-clock\n17\t  DEADLINE for the whole call, and measured spend checked between steps; a breach\n18\t  returns a typed `BudgetExceeded`, never a crash (ADR-004).\n19\t- **Telemetry.** One JSONL line per LLM request and one per run, written whether\n20\t  the run answered or tripped a budget (ADR-005) — a run that costs money and\n21\t  reports nothing is the one you most need the record of.\n22\t\n23\tThe system prompt is the FROZEN file `prompts/system.md`, read byte-exact by\n24\t`harness.prompt` and generated from `contract/` by `prompts/build_prompt.py`\n25\t(ADR-006). Nothing request-scoped is interpolated into it, and instructions are\n26\tmarked cacheable when the real Anthropic provider is in use.\n27\t\n28\t## The two paths\n29\t\n30\t`build_agent()` + old `ask(agent, deps, question, ...)` — the legacy tool-loop\n31\tpath. Tests and eval replay that script a `FunctionModel` use this path. It is\n32\tkept intact for backward compatibility.\n33\t\n34\tNew `ask(deps, question, ...)` (no `agent` argument) — the 4-stage pipeline:\n35\t1. `interpret_intent()` — LLM, no tools → StructuredIntent\n36\t2. `plan_and_execute()` — deterministic → envelope or typed refusal\n37\t3. `build_answer_view()` — deterministic → AnswerView\n38\t4. `narrate()` — LLM, no tools → NarrationOutput\n39\t\"\"\"\n40\t\n41\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n42\t\n43\timport asyncio\n44\timport logging\n45\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n46\tfrom typing import Any\n47\t\n48\tfrom anthropic import AsyncAnthropic\n49\tfrom pydantic_ai import Agent, ModelRetry, RunContext\n50\tfrom pydantic_ai.exceptions import UsageLimitExceeded\n51\tfrom pydantic_ai.models.anthropic import AnthropicModel, AnthropicModelSettings\n52\tfrom pydantic_ai.providers.anthropic import AnthropicProvider\n53\tfrom pydantic_ai.usage import UsageLimits\n54\t\n55\tfrom config import settings\n56\tfrom harness import contract, rendering, usage\n57\tfrom harness.claude_account_cli import build_claude_account_model\n58\tfrom harness.evidence import EvidenceClient\n59\tfrom harness.outputs import (\n60\t    AgentOutput,\n61\t    AnswerDraft,\n62\t    BudgetExceeded,\n63\t    ClarificationNeeded,\n64\t    HarnessOutput,\n65\t    RenderedAnswer,\n66\t    Unsupported,\n67\t)\n68\tfrom harness.prompt import system_prompt\n69\tfrom harness.retry import acall_with_tenacity\n70\tfrom harness.tools import (\n71\t    Deps,\n72\t    RepairCapExceeded,\n73\t    UnsupportedSignal,\n74\t    refusal_reason_is_contract_text,\n75\t    register_tools,\n76\t)\n77\t\n78\tlogger = logging.getLogger(\"harness.agent\")\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tclass SpendExceeded(Exception):\n82\t    \"\"\"Measured spend passed `settings.LOOP_MAX_USD` between steps (O-7).\n83\t\n84\t    Not a `HarnessError`, so the retry owner classifies it as unknown and\n85\t    re-raises it unchanged — retrying a run that has already spent its budget is\n86\t    the one thing that must not happen here.\n87\t    \"\"\"\n88\t\n89\t    def __init__(self, spent_usd: float, complete: bool) -> None:\n90\t        super().__init__(f\"spent ${spent_usd:.4f} of ${settings.LOOP_MAX_USD:.2f}\")\n91\t        self.spent_usd = spent_usd\n92\t        self.complete = complete\n93\t\n94\t\n95\tdef build_anthropic_client() -> AsyncAnthropic:\n96\t    \"\"\"The one place a real provider client is constructed (ADR-011, three modes).\n97\t\n98\t    `settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_MODE` follows the SDK's own resolution order, so the\n99\t    harness and the SDK can never disagree about which credential is in play:\n100\t\n101\t    | mode      | source                | how the client is built             |\n102\t    |---|---|---|\n103\t    | `api_key` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`   | `AsyncAnthropic(api_key=...)`       |\n104\t    | `account` | `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`| `AsyncAnthropic(auth_token=...)` + the OAuth beta header |\n105\t    | `profile` | neither is set        | `AsyncAnthropic()` — the SDK reads an `ant auth login` profile (or WIF env vars) itself |\n106\t\n107\t    **Profile mode passes no credential at all**, on purpose: the SDK resolves\n108\t    and refreshes the profile, and a harness that copied the token out of it\n109\t    would hold a stale one the moment it rotated.\n110\t\n111\t    **This is `ant auth login`, not `claude auth login`.** They are different\n112\t    CLIs with different credential stores; `claude auth login` (Claude Code)\n113\t    writes to neither the env vars above nor the profile file the SDK's\n114\t    zero-arg constructor reads (verified against\n115\t    `anthropic.lib.credentials._chain.default_credentials` in the installed\n116\t    SDK). A Claude Code / claude.ai session bridges into this client only via\n117\t    `claude setup-token`, which mints an explicit `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` — i.e.\n118\t    `account` mode, not `profile` mode. `run.require_credentials()` and\n119\t    `authcheck.py` both check the SDK's own resolver rather than which CLI\n120\t    binary happens to be on PATH, for exactly this reason.\n121\t\n122\t    `max_retries=0` in every mode — `harness.retry` is the single retry owner\n123\t    (ADR-003), and a second layer underneath it would multiply the attempt count\n124\t    and the wall clock without appearing anywhere in the deadline arithmetic.\n125\t    \"\"\"\n126\t    common: dict[str, Any] = {\"max_retries\": settings.ANTHROPIC_MAX_RETRIES}\n127\t    if settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_MODE == \"api_key\":\n128\t        return AsyncAnthropic(api_key=settings.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, **common)\n129\t    if settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_MODE == \"account\":\n130\t        # An OAuth bearer token on the Messages API needs this beta header; an\n131\t        # API key does not, and must not carry it. Without it the token is\n132\t        # rejected as an invalid bearer token, which reads as a bad credential\n133\t        # rather than as a missing header.\n134\t        return AsyncAnthropic(\n135\t            auth_token=settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN,\n136\t            default_headers={\"anthropic-beta\": settings.ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_BETA},\n137\t            **common,\n138\t        )\n139\t    return AsyncAnthropic(**common)\n140\t\n141\t\n142\tdef build_agent(\n143\t    model: object | None = None, instructions: str | None = None\n144\t) -> Agent[Deps, AgentOutput]:\n145\t    \"\"\"Wire provider, model, output union, tools and the rendering gate.\n146\t\n147\t    `model` and `instructions` are the injection points for tests and evals: pass\n148\t    a pydantic-ai `FunctionModel` to exercise the real tool wiring, the real\n149\t    subprocess emitter and the real validators with no network and no credentials.\n150\t    The frozen prompt is the default, so what the eval tier exercises is what\n151\t    ships (ADR-006).\n152\t\n153\t    This builds the LEGACY tool-loop agent. For the 4-stage pipeline, use the\n154\t    new `ask(deps, question)` signature (no `agent` argument).\n155\t    \"\"\"\n156\t    model_settings: AnthropicModelSettings | None = None\n157\t    if model is None:\n158\t        if settings.MODEL_PROVIDER == \"claude_account\":\n159\t            model = build_claude_account_model(\n160\t                binary=settings.CLAUDE_CLI,\n161\t                model=settings.CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL,\n162\t                timeout_seconds=settings.CLAUDE_CLI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS,\n163\t            )\n164\t        else:\n165\t            client = build_anthropic_client()\n166\t            model = AnthropicModel(\n167\t                settings.ANTHROPIC_MODEL,\n168\t                provider=AnthropicProvider(anthropic_client=client),\n169\t            )\n170\t            # The whole point of freezing the prompt (ADR-006). Provider-specific,\n171\t            # so it is set only where a real Anthropic model is wired.\n172\t            model_settings = AnthropicModelSettings(\n173\t                anthropic_cache_instructions=True,\n174\t                anthropic_cache_tool_definitions=True,\n175\t            )\n176\t\n177\t    agent: Agent[Deps, AgentOutput] = Agent(\n178\t        model,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n179\t        deps_type=Deps,\n180\t        output_type=AgentOutput,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n181\t        instructions=instructions if instructions is not None else system_prompt(),\n182\t        model_settings=model_settings,\n183\t    )\n184\t\n185\t    register_tools(agent)\n186\t\n187\t    @agent.output_validator\n188\t    def gate(ctx: RunContext[Deps], output: AgentOutput) -> AgentOutput:\n189\t        problems = _validate(ctx.deps, output)\n190\t        if problems:\n191\t            ctx.deps.output_validation_failures.append(problems)\n192\t            logger.warning(\n193\t                \"model output rejected by rendering gate\",\n194\t                extra={\n195\t                    \"subsystem\": \"model\",\n196\t                    \"output_branch\": type(output).__name__,\n197\t                    \"validation_problems\": problems,\n198\t                },\n199\t            )\n200\t            raise ModelRetry(\" \".join(problems))\n201\t        return output\n202\t\n203\t    return agent\n204\t\n205\t\n206\tdef _validate(deps: Deps, output: AgentOutput) -> list[str]:\n207\t    \"\"\"The branch-specific gates. Returns violations; empty means it stands.\"\"\"\n208\t    if isinstance(output, AnswerDraft):\n209\t        if deps.last_envelope is None:\n210\t            return [\n211\t                \"You have not fetched any evidence, so there is nothing to answer from. \"\n212\t                \"Call fetch_evidence, or return Unsupported if the contract excludes this.\"\n213\t            ]\n214\t        return rendering.validate_answer(\n215\t            answer=output.answer,\n216\t            data_status_note=output.data_status_note,\n217\t            question_id=output.question_id,\n218\t            envelope=deps.last_envelope,\n219\t            user_question=deps.user_question,\n220\t        )\n221\t\n222\t    if isinstance(output, ClarificationNeeded):\n223\t        problems = []\n224\t        if deps.last_envelope is not None:\n225\t            problems.append(\n226\t                \"You already have evidence for this question. Answer it rather than asking.\"\n227\t            )\n228\t        if not output.missing:\n229\t            problems.append(\"ClarificationNeeded must name at least one missing input.\")\n230\t        # The materials gate (architecture §7): the model can neither skip asking\n231\t        # for a material input nor burn a turn asking about defaultable trivia.\n232\t        material = contract.material_inputs_for(output.question_id)\n233\t        overreach = [m.input for m in output.missing if m.input not in material]\n234\t        if overreach:\n235\t            problems.append(\n236\t                f\"These inputs are not material for {output.question_id} and are defaulted \"\n237\t                f\"by the data layer: {overreach}. Use the defaults and report the values \"\n238\t                \"that were applied, from the envelope's filters.\"\n239\t            )\n240\t        return problems\n241\t\n242\t    if isinstance(output, Unsupported):\n243\t        # `unanswerable` is a fact returned by the evidence layer for a valid\n244\t        # request, never a model judgement. The tool converts that error into an\n245\t        # UnsupportedSignal before output validation, so any instance reaching\n246\t        # this branch was invented without evidence (the VC-POC-03 live miss).\n247\t        if output.reason_kind == \"unanswerable\":\n248\t            return [\n249\t                \"Only the evidence layer may determine that a valid request is \"\n250\t                \"unanswerable. Resolve named schools with search_schools and call \"\n251\t                \"fetch_evidence before abstaining.\"\n252\t            ]\n253\t        if not refusal_reason_is_contract_text(output):\n254\t            return [\n255\t                \"A contract refusal must use the contract's own wording. Use the exclusion \"\n256\t                \"text from the registry or from the emitter's error, not your own phrasing.\"\n257\t            ]\n258\t    return []\n259\t\n260\t\n261\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n262\t# Legacy tool-loop ask() — for backward compat with tests and evals\n263\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n264\t\n265\t\n266\tasync def ask(  # type: ignore[return]\n267\t    agent_or_deps: Any,\n268\t    deps_or_question: Any = None,\n269\t    question_or_record_usage: Any = None,\n270\t    message_history: list[Any] | None = None,\n271\t    record_usage: bool = True,\n272\t    *,\n273\t    # New pipeline-only keyword arguments\n274\t    intent_override: Any = None,\n275\t    narration_override: Any = None,\n276\t    intent_model: object | None = None,\n277\t    narration_model: object | None = None,\n278\t) -> HarnessOutput:\n279\t    \"\"\"Run one question through the harness.\n280\t\n281\t    Two call signatures are supported:\n282\t\n283\t    **Legacy (tool-loop) path** — for backward compat with tests and evals:\n284\t        ask(agent, deps, question, message_history=None, record_usage=True)\n285\t\n286\t    **New pipeline path** — 4-stage pipeline with no `agent` argument:\n287\t        ask(deps, question, record_usage=True, *, intent_override=None, ...)\n288\t\n289\t    The legacy path is detected by checking whether `agent_or_deps` is an\n290\t    `Agent` instance (it would be `Deps` in the new path). Both paths share\n291\t    the same budget model and telemetry.\n292\t    \"\"\"\n293\t    # Detect the call signature\n294\t    if isinstance(agent_or_deps, Agent):\n295\t        # Legacy signature: ask(agent, deps, question, ...)\n296\t        agent: Agent[Deps, AgentOutput] = agent_or_deps\n297\t        deps: Deps = deps_or_question\n298\t        question: str = question_or_record_usage\n299\t        # record_usage is the keyword arg or the positional default\n300\t        return await _ask_legacy(\n301\t            agent=agent,\n302\t            deps=deps,\n303\t            question=question,\n304\t            message_history=message_history,\n305\t            record_usage=record_usage,\n306\t        )\n307\t    else:\n308\t        # New signature: ask(deps, question, record_usage=True, ...)\n309\t        deps = agent_or_deps\n310\t        question = deps_or_question\n311\t        if question_or_record_usage is not None:\n312\t            # Positional record_usage in the new signature\n313\t            record_usage = bool(question_or_record_usage)\n314\t        return await _ask_pipeline(\n315\t            deps=deps,\n316\t            question=question,\n317\t            record_usage=record_usage,\n318\t            intent_override=intent_override,\n319\t            narration_override=narration_override,\n320\t            intent_model=intent_model,\n321\t            narration_model=narration_model,\n322\t        )\n323\t\n324\t\n325\tasync def _ask_legacy(\n326\t    agent: Agent[Deps, AgentOutput],\n327\t    deps: Deps,\n328\t    question: str,\n329\t    message_history: list[Any] | None = None,\n330\t    record_usage: bool = True,\n331\t) -> HarnessOutput:\n332\t    \"\"\"Run one question under the control envelope using the legacy tool loop.\n333\t\n334\t    Budgets are enforced here, in code (ADR-004) — all four:\n335\t\n336\t    | budget | mechanism |\n337\t    |---|---|\n338\t    | steps / tool calls | `UsageLimits` |\n339\t    | wall clock | ONE deadline for the whole call, shared across retry attempts |\n340\t    | spend | measured between steps from the run's own message history |\n341\t\n342\t    A breach returns a typed `BudgetExceeded` carrying what the run had\n343\t    established — never a crash, and never a partial answer.\n344\t\n345\t    **The deadline is the whole call, not one attempt** (closes O-9). The\n346\t    previous shape put `wait_for(LOOP_MAX_SECONDS)` *inside* the retry owner, so\n347\t    a run that kept hitting 429s could spend `MAX_ATTEMPTS x LOOP_MAX_SECONDS`\n348\t    plus backoff while still reporting the single-attempt figure. Here the\n349\t    deadline is computed once and each attempt gets only the time left; an\n350\t    attempt that starts past it times out immediately.\n351\t\n352\t    `message_history` carries a clarification round-trip: the caller presents\n353\t    `prompt_to_user`, collects the reply, and re-invokes with the prior history\n354\t    plus the answer. PydanticAI's message history is the whole session store the\n355\t    POC needs (architecture §7).\n356\t    \"\"\"\n357\t    deps.user_question = question\n358\t    limits = UsageLimits(\n359\t        request_limit=settings.LOOP_MAX_STEPS,\n360\t        tool_calls_limit=settings.LOOP_MAX_TOOL_CALLS,\n361\t    )\n362\t    loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n363\t    deadline = loop.time() + settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS\n364\t    started_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n365\t    # The run object, captured so telemetry survives a budget trip: an aborted\n366\t    # run is exactly the one whose cost you need on record (ADR-005).\n367\t    runs: list[Any] = []\n368\t\n369\t    async def _iterate() -> Any:\n370\t        async with agent.iter(\n371\t            question,\n372\t            deps=deps,\n373\t            usage_limits=limits,\n374\t            message_history=message_history,\n375\t        ) as run:\n376\t            runs.append(run)\n377\t            async for _node in run:\n378\t                _check_spend(run)\n379\t            return run.result\n380\t\n381\t    async def _run() -> Any:\n382\t        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n383\t        if remaining <= 0:\n384\t            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n385\t        return await asyncio.wait_for(_iterate(), timeout=remaining)\n386\t\n387\t    def done(output: HarnessOutput) -> HarnessOutput:\n388\t        \"\"\"Every exit from this function goes through here, so no branch can\n389\t        return without handing back its history and its usage record.\"\"\"\n390\t        return _finish(output, runs, question, started_at, record_usage, deps)\n391\t\n392\t    try:\n393\t        result = await acall_with_tenacity(_run)\n394\t    except UnsupportedSignal as exc:\n395\t        # The refusal short-circuit: an excluded or unknown question ends the run\n396\t        # as an answer in its own right, never as an error and never as a retry.\n397\t        return done(exc.unsupported)\n398\t    except RepairCapExceeded as exc:\n399\t        # v0.2.0 classifies four unrepairable failures as `bad_request`. After the\n400\t        # cap, the honest outcome is a refusal quoting the data layer's own\n401\t        # message — not another attempt, and not a fabricated answer.\n402\t        return done(\n403\t            Unsupported(reason_kind=\"out_of_scope\", reason=exc.message, nearest_supported=None)\n404\t        )\n405\t    except SpendExceeded as exc:\n406\t        detail = f\"{exc} (measured cost{'' if exc.complete else ', lower bound'})\"\n407\t        return done(\n408\t            BudgetExceeded(limit=\"usd\", detail=detail, learned_so_far=_learned(deps))\n409\t        )\n410\t    except UsageLimitExceeded as exc:\n411\t        return done(\n412\t            BudgetExceeded(\n413\t                limit=\"tool_calls\" if \"tool\" in str(exc).lower() else \"steps\",\n414\t                detail=str(exc),\n415\t                learned_so_far=_learned(deps),\n416\t            )\n417\t        )\n418\t    except asyncio.TimeoutError:\n419\t        return done(\n420\t            BudgetExceeded(\n421\t                limit=\"seconds\",\n422\t                detail=f\"exceeded {settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS}s wall clock for the whole call\",\n423\t                learned_so_far=_learned(deps),\n424\t            )\n425\t        )\n426\t\n427\t    output = result.output\n428\t    if isinstance(output, AnswerDraft):\n429\t        assert deps.last_envelope is not None  # guaranteed by the output validator\n430\t        output = RenderedAnswer.from_envelope(output, deps.last_envelope)\n431\t    return done(output)\n432\t\n433\t\n434\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n435\t# New 4-stage pipeline ask()\n436\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n437\t\n438\t\n439\tasync def _ask_pipeline(\n440\t    deps: Deps,\n441\t    question: str,\n442\t    record_usage: bool = True,\n443\t    *,\n444\t    intent_override: Any = None,\n445\t    narration_override: Any = None,\n446\t    intent_model: object | None = None,\n447\t    narration_model: object | None = None,\n448\t) -> HarnessOutput:\n449\t    \"\"\"Run one question through the 4-stage pipeline.\n450\t\n451\t    Stage 1: Intent interpretation (LLM, no tools) → StructuredIntent\n452\t    Stage 2: Deterministic planning/execution (code) → envelope or typed refusal\n453\t    Stage 3: Deterministic answer view (code) → AnswerView\n454\t    Stage 4: Optional narration (LLM, no tools) → NarrationOutput → RenderedAnswer\n455\t\n456\t    Budget handling wraps the whole pipeline: the wall-clock deadline, the spend\n457\t    budget, and a BudgetExceeded are the same typed outcome as the legacy path.\n458\t    \"\"\"\n459\t    # Deferred imports to avoid circular import at module load time\n460\t    from harness.answer_view import build_answer_view\n461\t    from harness.intent import interpret_intent\n462\t    from harness.narration import _validate_narration, narrate\n463\t    from harness.planner import plan_and_execute\n464\t\n465\t    deps.user_question = question\n466\t    loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n467\t    deadline = loop.time() + settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS\n468\t    started_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n469\t    runs: list[Any] = []  # empty in pipeline mode; telemetry records differently\n470\t\n471\t    def done(output: HarnessOutput) -> HarnessOutput:\n472\t        return _finish(output, runs, question, started_at, record_usage, deps)\n473\t\n474\t    try:\n475\t        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n476\t        if remaining <= 0:\n477\t            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n478\t\n479\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n480\t        # Stage 1: Intent interpretation\n481\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n482\t        if intent_override is not None:\n483\t            intent = intent_override\n484\t        else:\n485\t            intent = await asyncio.wait_for(\n486\t                interpret_intent(question, model=intent_model),\n487\t                timeout=remaining,\n488\t            )\n489\t        deps.intent = intent\n490\t\n491\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n492\t        # Stage 2: Plan and execute\n493\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n494\t        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n495\t        if remaining <= 0:\n496\t            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n497\t\n498\t        result = await asyncio.wait_for(\n499\t            plan_and_execute(intent, deps.client, deps),\n500\t            timeout=remaining,\n501\t        )\n502\t\n503\t        if isinstance(result, (ClarificationNeeded, Unsupported)):\n504\t            return done(result)\n505\t\n506\t        # result is the evidence envelope (dict)\n507\t        envelope = result\n508\t\n509\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n510\t        # Stage 3: Build answer view\n511\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n512\t        view = build_answer_view(envelope)\n513\t        deps.answer_view = view\n514\t\n515\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n516\t        # Stage 4: Narration\n517\t        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n518\t        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n519\t        if remaining <= 0:\n520\t            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n521\t\n522\t        if narration_override is not None:\n523\t            narration = narration_override\n524\t            _validate_narration(view, deps, narration)\n525\t        else:\n526\t            narration = await asyncio.wait_for(\n527\t                narrate(view, deps, model=narration_model),\n528\t                timeout=remaining,\n529\t            )\n530\t\n531\t        # Assemble the RenderedAnswer from the view + narration\n532\t        output: HarnessOutput = RenderedAnswer(\n533\t            answer=narration.answer,\n534\t            question_id=view.question_id,\n535\t            contract_version=view.contract_version,\n536\t            evidence=view.evidence,\n537\t            provenance=view.provenance,\n538\t            confidence=view.confidence,\n539\t            limitations=view.limitations,\n540\t            deterministic_signals=view.deterministic_signals,\n541\t            resolved_request=view.resolved_request,\n542\t            data_status=view.data_status,\n543\t            claim_eligibility=view.claim_eligibility,\n544\t            data_status_note=view.data_status_note,\n545\t        )\n546\t        return done(output)\n547\t\n548\t    except SpendExceeded as exc:\n549\t        detail = f\"{exc} (measured cost{'' if exc.complete else ', lower bound'})\"\n550\t        return done(\n551\t            BudgetExceeded(limit=\"usd\", detail=detail, learned_so_far=_learned(deps))\n552\t        )\n553\t    except asyncio.TimeoutError:\n554\t        return done(\n555\t            BudgetExceeded(\n556\t                limit=\"seconds\",\n557\t                detail=f\"exceeded {settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS}s wall clock for the whole call\",\n558\t                learned_so_far=_learned(deps),\n559\t            )\n560\t        )\n561\t\n562\t\n563\tdef _check_spend(run: Any) -> None:\n564\t    \"\"\"Trip the spend budget BETWEEN steps (closes O-7).\n565\t\n566\t    Between steps is the only place it can be enforced: the cost of a request is\n567\t    only knowable once its response has arrived, so the budget stops the *next*\n568\t    request rather than the one that crossed the line. `LOOP_MAX_USD` is\n569\t    therefore a ceiling on what a run may commit to spending, not a hard cap on\n570\t    what it has spent — size it accordingly.\n571\t    \"\"\"\n572\t    spent, complete = usage.spend_usd(run.all_messages())\n573\t    if spent > settings.LOOP_MAX_USD:\n574\t        logger.warning(\n575\t            \"spend budget exceeded\",\n576\t            extra={\n577\t                \"subsystem\": \"api\",\n578\t                \"spent_usd\": spent,\n579\t                \"limit_usd\": settings.LOOP_MAX_USD,\n580\t                \"cost_complete\": complete,\n581\t            },\n582\t        )\n583\t        raise SpendExceeded(spent, complete)\n584\t\n585\t\n586\tdef _finish(\n587\t    output: HarnessOutput,\n588\t    runs: list[Any],\n589\t    question: str,\n590\t    started_at: datetime,\n591\t    record_usage: bool,\n592\t    deps: Deps,\n593\t) -> HarnessOutput:\n594\t    \"\"\"Hand the message history back to the caller, write the usage records, and\n595\t    return the outcome unchanged.\n596\t\n597\t    The history goes onto `deps` on EVERY branch, including a budget trip: a\n598\t    caller that wants to answer a clarification needs it, and a caller\n599\t    inspecting a failed run needs it more. Telemetry never alters or fails a\n600\t    result — `record_run` swallows its own errors (ADR-005). `runs` is empty\n601\t    only when the agent never started (pipeline mode uses no agent).\n602\t    \"\"\"\n603\t    if runs:\n604\t        deps.last_messages = list(runs[-1].all_messages())\n605\t        if record_usage:\n606\t            usage.record_run(\n607\t                runs[-1],\n608\t                question=question,\n609\t                output_branch=type(output).__name__,\n610\t                started_at=started_at,\n611\t            )\n612\t    return output\n613\t\n614\t\n615\tdef _learned(deps: Deps) -> str:\n616\t    \"\"\"What a budget breach can still tell the caller. Never a partial answer —\n617\t    a half-rendered figure is worse than none.\"\"\"\n618\t    parts = []\n619\t    if deps.resolved_school_ids:\n620\t        parts.append(f\"resolved school IDs {deps.resolved_school_ids}\")\n621\t    if deps.last_envelope is not None:\n622\t        parts.append(f\"fetched evidence for {deps.last_envelope['question_id']}\")\n623\t    if deps.repair_attempts:\n624\t        parts.append(f\"{deps.repair_attempts} request repair attempt(s)\")\n625\t    return \"; \".join(parts)\n626\t\n627\t\n628\tdef build_deps(client: EvidenceClient | None = None) -> Deps:\n629\t    return Deps(client=client or EvidenceClient.from_settings())\n630\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e8b7dde-8bb0-4345-aaad-7bcee95758ae","uuid":"bef47cbe-d12d-4ee1-85f0-ad572aafaf43","timestamp":"2026-09-26T09:59:54.450Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/harness/agent.py","content":"\"\"\"Agent assembly: provider wiring, the output union, the rendering gate, budgets.\n\nWhat this module is responsible for, and nothing else:\n\n- **Provider wiring.** The local POC defaults to the token-backed Claude Code\n  subscription account; the Anthropic SDK remains an explicit, potentially\n  metered transport. SDK retries are 0 —\n  `harness.retry` is the single retry owner (ADR-003).\n- **The output union.** The model chooses between `AnswerDraft`,\n  `ClarificationNeeded` and `Unsupported`; `ask()` widens that to\n  `HarnessOutput` by attaching the preserved envelope fields and by adding the\n  `BudgetExceeded` branch the model can never select (architecture §5).\n- **The rendering gate.** An output validator applies `harness.rendering` and\n  hands violations back as `ModelRetry`, so a run self-corrects rather than\n  returning something the eval suite would fail later.\n- **The control envelope.** `UsageLimits` for steps and tool calls, one wall-clock\n  DEADLINE for the whole call, and measured spend checked between steps; a breach\n  returns a typed `BudgetExceeded`, never a crash (ADR-004).\n- **Telemetry.** One JSONL line per LLM request and one per run, written whether\n  the run answered or tripped a budget (ADR-005) — a run that costs money and\n  reports nothing is the one you most need the record of.\n\nThe system prompt is the FROZEN file `prompts/system.md`, read byte-exact by\n`harness.prompt` and generated from `contract/` by `prompts/build_prompt.py`\n(ADR-006). Nothing request-scoped is interpolated into it, and instructions are\nmarked cacheable when the real Anthropic provider is in use.\n\n## The two paths\n\n`build_agent()` + old `ask(agent, deps, question, ...)` — the legacy tool-loop\npath. Tests and eval replay that script a `FunctionModel` use this path. It is\nkept intact for backward compatibility.\n\nNew `ask(deps, question, ...)` (no `agent` argument) — the 4-stage pipeline:\n1. `interpret_intent()` — LLM, no tools → StructuredIntent\n2. `plan_and_execute()` — deterministic → envelope or typed refusal\n3. `build_answer_view()` — deterministic → AnswerView\n4. `narrate()` — LLM, no tools → NarrationOutput\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport logging\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom anthropic import AsyncAnthropic\nfrom pydantic_ai import Agent, ModelRetry, RunContext\nfrom pydantic_ai.exceptions import UsageLimitExceeded\nfrom pydantic_ai.models.anthropic import AnthropicModel, AnthropicModelSettings\nfrom pydantic_ai.providers.anthropic import AnthropicProvider\nfrom pydantic_ai.usage import UsageLimits\n\nfrom config import settings\nfrom harness import contract, rendering, usage\nfrom harness.claude_account_cli import build_claude_account_model\nfrom harness.evidence import EvidenceClient\nfrom harness.outputs import (\n    AgentOutput,\n    AnswerDraft,\n    BudgetExceeded,\n    ClarificationNeeded,\n    HarnessOutput,\n    RenderedAnswer,\n    Unsupported,\n)\nfrom harness.prompt import system_prompt\nfrom harness.retry import acall_with_tenacity\nfrom harness.tools import (\n    Deps,\n    RepairCapExceeded,\n    UnsupportedSignal,\n    refusal_reason_is_contract_text,\n    register_tools,\n)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"harness.agent\")\n\n\nclass SpendExceeded(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Measured spend passed `settings.LOOP_MAX_USD` between steps (O-7).\n\n    Not a `HarnessError`, so the retry owner classifies it as unknown and\n    re-raises it unchanged — retrying a run that has already spent its budget is\n    the one thing that must not happen here.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, spent_usd: float, complete: bool) -> None:\n        super().__init__(f\"spent ${spent_usd:.4f} of ${settings.LOOP_MAX_USD:.2f}\")\n        self.spent_usd = spent_usd\n        self.complete = complete\n\n\ndef build_anthropic_client() -> AsyncAnthropic:\n    \"\"\"The one place a real provider client is constructed (ADR-011, three modes).\n\n    `settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_MODE` follows the SDK's own resolution order, so the\n    harness and the SDK can never disagree about which credential is in play:\n\n    | mode      | source                | how the client is built             |\n    |---|---|---|\n    | `api_key` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`   | `AsyncAnthropic(api_key=...)`       |\n    | `account` | `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`| `AsyncAnthropic(auth_token=...)` + the OAuth beta header |\n    | `profile` | neither is set        | `AsyncAnthropic()` — the SDK reads an `ant auth login` profile (or WIF env vars) itself |\n\n    **Profile mode passes no credential at all**, on purpose: the SDK resolves\n    and refreshes the profile, and a harness that copied the token out of it\n    would hold a stale one the moment it rotated.\n\n    **This is `ant auth login`, not `claude auth login`.** They are different\n    CLIs with different credential stores; `claude auth login` (Claude Code)\n    writes to neither the env vars above nor the profile file the SDK's\n    zero-arg constructor reads (verified against\n    `anthropic.lib.credentials._chain.default_credentials` in the installed\n    SDK). A Claude Code / claude.ai session bridges into this client only via\n    `claude setup-token`, which mints an explicit `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` — i.e.\n    `account` mode, not `profile` mode. `run.require_credentials()` and\n    `authcheck.py` both check the SDK's own resolver rather than which CLI\n    binary happens to be on PATH, for exactly this reason.\n\n    `max_retries=0` in every mode — `harness.retry` is the single retry owner\n    (ADR-003), and a second layer underneath it would multiply the attempt count\n    and the wall clock without appearing anywhere in the deadline arithmetic.\n    \"\"\"\n    common: dict[str, Any] = {\"max_retries\": settings.ANTHROPIC_MAX_RETRIES}\n    if settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_MODE == \"api_key\":\n        return AsyncAnthropic(api_key=settings.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, **common)\n    if settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_MODE == \"account\":\n        # An OAuth bearer token on the Messages API needs this beta header; an\n        # API key does not, and must not carry it. Without it the token is\n        # rejected as an invalid bearer token, which reads as a bad credential\n        # rather than as a missing header.\n        return AsyncAnthropic(\n            auth_token=settings.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN,\n            default_headers={\"anthropic-beta\": settings.ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_BETA},\n            **common,\n        )\n    return AsyncAnthropic(**common)\n\n\ndef build_agent(\n    model: object | None = None, instructions: str | None = None\n) -> Agent[Deps, AgentOutput]:\n    \"\"\"Wire provider, model, output union, tools and the rendering gate.\n\n    `model` and `instructions` are the injection points for tests and evals: pass\n    a pydantic-ai `FunctionModel` to exercise the real tool wiring, the real\n    subprocess emitter and the real validators with no network and no credentials.\n    The frozen prompt is the default, so what the eval tier exercises is what\n    ships (ADR-006).\n\n    This builds the LEGACY tool-loop agent. For the 4-stage pipeline, use the\n    new `ask(deps, question)` signature (no `agent` argument).\n    \"\"\"\n    model_settings: AnthropicModelSettings | None = None\n    if model is None:\n        if settings.MODEL_PROVIDER == \"claude_account\":\n            model = build_claude_account_model(\n                binary=settings.CLAUDE_CLI,\n                model=settings.CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL,\n                timeout_seconds=settings.CLAUDE_CLI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS,\n            )\n        else:\n            client = build_anthropic_client()\n            model = AnthropicModel(\n                settings.ANTHROPIC_MODEL,\n                provider=AnthropicProvider(anthropic_client=client),\n            )\n            # The whole point of freezing the prompt (ADR-006). Provider-specific,\n            # so it is set only where a real Anthropic model is wired.\n            model_settings = AnthropicModelSettings(\n                anthropic_cache_instructions=True,\n                anthropic_cache_tool_definitions=True,\n            )\n\n    agent: Agent[Deps, AgentOutput] = Agent(\n        model,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n        deps_type=Deps,\n        output_type=AgentOutput,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n        instructions=instructions if instructions is not None else system_prompt(),\n        model_settings=model_settings,\n    )\n\n    register_tools(agent)\n\n    @agent.output_validator\n    def gate(ctx: RunContext[Deps], output: AgentOutput) -> AgentOutput:\n        problems = _validate(ctx.deps, output)\n        if problems:\n            ctx.deps.output_validation_failures.append(problems)\n            logger.warning(\n                \"model output rejected by rendering gate\",\n                extra={\n                    \"subsystem\": \"model\",\n                    \"output_branch\": type(output).__name__,\n                    \"validation_problems\": problems,\n                },\n            )\n            raise ModelRetry(\" \".join(problems))\n        return output\n\n    return agent\n\n\ndef _validate(deps: Deps, output: AgentOutput) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"The branch-specific gates. Returns violations; empty means it stands.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(output, AnswerDraft):\n        if deps.last_envelope is None:\n            return [\n                \"You have not fetched any evidence, so there is nothing to answer from. \"\n                \"Call fetch_evidence, or return Unsupported if the contract excludes this.\"\n            ]\n        return rendering.validate_answer(\n            answer=output.answer,\n            data_status_note=output.data_status_note,\n            question_id=output.question_id,\n            envelope=deps.last_envelope,\n            user_question=deps.user_question,\n        )\n\n    if isinstance(output, ClarificationNeeded):\n        problems = []\n        if deps.last_envelope is not None:\n            problems.append(\n                \"You already have evidence for this question. Answer it rather than asking.\"\n            )\n        if not output.missing:\n            problems.append(\"ClarificationNeeded must name at least one missing input.\")\n        # The materials gate (architecture §7): the model can neither skip asking\n        # for a material input nor burn a turn asking about defaultable trivia.\n        material = contract.material_inputs_for(output.question_id)\n        overreach = [m.input for m in output.missing if m.input not in material]\n        if overreach:\n            problems.append(\n                f\"These inputs are not material for {output.question_id} and are defaulted \"\n                f\"by the data layer: {overreach}. Use the defaults and report the values \"\n                \"that were applied, from the envelope's filters.\"\n            )\n        return problems\n\n    if isinstance(output, Unsupported):\n        # `unanswerable` is a fact returned by the evidence layer for a valid\n        # request, never a model judgement. The tool converts that error into an\n        # UnsupportedSignal before output validation, so any instance reaching\n        # this branch was invented without evidence (the VC-POC-03 live miss).\n        if output.reason_kind == \"unanswerable\":\n            return [\n                \"Only the evidence layer may determine that a valid request is \"\n                \"unanswerable. Resolve named schools with search_schools and call \"\n                \"fetch_evidence before abstaining.\"\n            ]\n        if not refusal_reason_is_contract_text(output):\n            return [\n                \"A contract refusal must use the contract's own wording. Use the exclusion \"\n                \"text from the registry or from the emitter's error, not your own phrasing.\"\n            ]\n    return []\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Legacy tool-loop ask() — for backward compat with tests and evals\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nasync def ask(  # type: ignore[return]\n    agent_or_deps: Any,\n    deps_or_question: Any = None,\n    question_or_record_usage: Any = None,\n    message_history: list[Any] | None = None,\n    record_usage: bool = True,\n    *,\n    # New pipeline-only keyword arguments\n    intent_override: Any = None,\n    narration_override: Any = None,\n    intent_model: object | None = None,\n    narration_model: object | None = None,\n) -> HarnessOutput:\n    \"\"\"Run one question through the harness.\n\n    Two call signatures are supported:\n\n    **Legacy (tool-loop) path** — for backward compat with tests and evals:\n        ask(agent, deps, question, message_history=None, record_usage=True)\n\n    **New pipeline path** — 4-stage pipeline with no `agent` argument:\n        ask(deps, question, record_usage=True, *, intent_override=None, ...)\n\n    The legacy path is detected by checking whether `agent_or_deps` is an\n    `Agent` instance (it would be `Deps` in the new path). Both paths share\n    the same budget model and telemetry.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Detect the call signature\n    if isinstance(agent_or_deps, Agent):\n        # Legacy signature: ask(agent, deps, question, ...)\n        agent: Agent[Deps, AgentOutput] = agent_or_deps\n        deps: Deps = deps_or_question\n        question: str = question_or_record_usage\n        # record_usage is the keyword arg or the positional default\n        return await _ask_legacy(\n            agent=agent,\n            deps=deps,\n            question=question,\n            message_history=message_history,\n            record_usage=record_usage,\n        )\n    else:\n        # New signature: ask(deps, question, record_usage=True, ...)\n        deps = agent_or_deps\n        question = deps_or_question\n        if question_or_record_usage is not None:\n            # Positional record_usage in the new signature\n            record_usage = bool(question_or_record_usage)\n        return await _ask_pipeline(\n            deps=deps,\n            question=question,\n            record_usage=record_usage,\n            intent_override=intent_override,\n            narration_override=narration_override,\n            intent_model=intent_model,\n            narration_model=narration_model,\n        )\n\n\nasync def _ask_legacy(\n    agent: Agent[Deps, AgentOutput],\n    deps: Deps,\n    question: str,\n    message_history: list[Any] | None = None,\n    record_usage: bool = True,\n) -> HarnessOutput:\n    \"\"\"Run one question under the control envelope using the legacy tool loop.\n\n    Budgets are enforced here, in code (ADR-004) — all four:\n\n    | budget | mechanism |\n    |---|---|\n    | steps / tool calls | `UsageLimits` |\n    | wall clock | ONE deadline for the whole call, shared across retry attempts |\n    | spend | measured between steps from the run's own message history |\n\n    A breach returns a typed `BudgetExceeded` carrying what the run had\n    established — never a crash, and never a partial answer.\n\n    **The deadline is the whole call, not one attempt** (closes O-9). The\n    previous shape put `wait_for(LOOP_MAX_SECONDS)` *inside* the retry owner, so\n    a run that kept hitting 429s could spend `MAX_ATTEMPTS x LOOP_MAX_SECONDS`\n    plus backoff while still reporting the single-attempt figure. Here the\n    deadline is computed once and each attempt gets only the time left; an\n    attempt that starts past it times out immediately.\n\n    `message_history` carries a clarification round-trip: the caller presents\n    `prompt_to_user`, collects the reply, and re-invokes with the prior history\n    plus the answer. PydanticAI's message history is the whole session store the\n    POC needs (architecture §7).\n    \"\"\"\n    deps.user_question = question\n    limits = UsageLimits(\n        request_limit=settings.LOOP_MAX_STEPS,\n        tool_calls_limit=settings.LOOP_MAX_TOOL_CALLS,\n    )\n    loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n    deadline = loop.time() + settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS\n    started_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n    # The run object, captured so telemetry survives a budget trip: an aborted\n    # run is exactly the one whose cost you need on record (ADR-005).\n    runs: list[Any] = []\n\n    async def _iterate() -> Any:\n        async with agent.iter(\n            question,\n            deps=deps,\n            usage_limits=limits,\n            message_history=message_history,\n        ) as run:\n            runs.append(run)\n            async for _node in run:\n                _check_spend(run)\n            return run.result\n\n    async def _run() -> Any:\n        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n        return await asyncio.wait_for(_iterate(), timeout=remaining)\n\n    def done(output: HarnessOutput) -> HarnessOutput:\n        \"\"\"Every exit from this function goes through here, so no branch can\n        return without handing back its history and its usage record.\"\"\"\n        return _finish(output, runs, question, started_at, record_usage, deps)\n\n    try:\n        result = await acall_with_tenacity(_run)\n    except UnsupportedSignal as exc:\n        # The refusal short-circuit: an excluded or unknown question ends the run\n        # as an answer in its own right, never as an error and never as a retry.\n        return done(exc.unsupported)\n    except RepairCapExceeded as exc:\n        # v0.2.0 classifies four unrepairable failures as `bad_request`. After the\n        # cap, the honest outcome is a refusal quoting the data layer's own\n        # message — not another attempt, and not a fabricated answer.\n        return done(\n            Unsupported(reason_kind=\"out_of_scope\", reason=exc.message, nearest_supported=None)\n        )\n    except SpendExceeded as exc:\n        detail = f\"{exc} (measured cost{'' if exc.complete else ', lower bound'})\"\n        return done(\n            BudgetExceeded(limit=\"usd\", detail=detail, learned_so_far=_learned(deps))\n        )\n    except UsageLimitExceeded as exc:\n        return done(\n            BudgetExceeded(\n                limit=\"tool_calls\" if \"tool\" in str(exc).lower() else \"steps\",\n                detail=str(exc),\n                learned_so_far=_learned(deps),\n            )\n        )\n    except asyncio.TimeoutError:\n        return done(\n            BudgetExceeded(\n                limit=\"seconds\",\n                detail=f\"exceeded {settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS}s wall clock for the whole call\",\n                learned_so_far=_learned(deps),\n            )\n        )\n\n    output = result.output\n    if isinstance(output, AnswerDraft):\n        assert deps.last_envelope is not None  # guaranteed by the output validator\n        output = RenderedAnswer.from_envelope(output, deps.last_envelope)\n    return done(output)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# New 4-stage pipeline ask()\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nasync def _ask_pipeline(\n    deps: Deps,\n    question: str,\n    record_usage: bool = True,\n    *,\n    intent_override: Any = None,\n    narration_override: Any = None,\n    intent_model: object | None = None,\n    narration_model: object | None = None,\n) -> HarnessOutput:\n    \"\"\"Run one question through the 4-stage pipeline.\n\n    Stage 1: Intent interpretation (LLM, no tools) → StructuredIntent\n    Stage 2: Deterministic planning/execution (code) → envelope or typed refusal\n    Stage 3: Deterministic answer view (code) → AnswerView\n    Stage 4: Optional narration (LLM, no tools) → NarrationOutput → RenderedAnswer\n\n    Budget handling wraps the whole pipeline: the wall-clock deadline, the spend\n    budget, and a BudgetExceeded are the same typed outcome as the legacy path.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Deferred imports to avoid circular import at module load time\n    from harness.answer_view import build_answer_view\n    from harness.intent import interpret_intent\n    from harness.narration import _validate_narration, narrate\n    from harness.planner import plan_and_execute\n\n    deps.user_question = question\n    loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()\n    deadline = loop.time() + settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS\n    started_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n    runs: list[Any] = []  # empty in pipeline mode; telemetry records differently\n\n    def done(output: HarnessOutput) -> HarnessOutput:\n        return _finish(output, runs, question, started_at, record_usage, deps)\n\n    try:\n        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        # Stage 1: Intent interpretation\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        if intent_override is not None:\n            intent = intent_override\n        else:\n            intent = await asyncio.wait_for(\n                interpret_intent(question, model=intent_model),\n                timeout=remaining,\n            )\n        deps.intent = intent\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        # Stage 2: Plan and execute\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n\n        result = await asyncio.wait_for(\n            plan_and_execute(intent, deps.client, deps),\n            timeout=remaining,\n        )\n\n        if isinstance(result, (ClarificationNeeded, Unsupported)):\n            return done(result)\n\n        # result is the evidence envelope (dict)\n        envelope = result\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        # Stage 3: Build answer view\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        view = build_answer_view(envelope)\n        deps.answer_view = view\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        # Stage 4: Narration\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------- #\n        remaining = deadline - loop.time()\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            raise asyncio.TimeoutError\n\n        if narration_override is not None:\n            narration = narration_override\n            _validate_narration(view, deps, narration)\n        else:\n            narration = await asyncio.wait_for(\n                narrate(view, deps, model=narration_model),\n                timeout=remaining,\n            )\n\n        # Assemble the RenderedAnswer from the view + narration\n        output: HarnessOutput = RenderedAnswer(\n            answer=narration.answer,\n            question_id=view.question_id,\n            contract_version=view.contract_version,\n            evidence=view.evidence,\n            provenance=view.provenance,\n            confidence=view.confidence,\n            limitations=view.limitations,\n            deterministic_signals=view.deterministic_signals,\n            resolved_request=view.resolved_request,\n            data_status=view.data_status,\n            claim_eligibility=view.claim_eligibility,\n            data_status_note=view.data_status_note,\n        )\n        return done(output)\n\n    except SpendExceeded as exc:\n        detail = f\"{exc} (measured cost{'' if exc.complete else ', lower bound'})\"\n        return done(\n            BudgetExceeded(limit=\"usd\", detail=detail, learned_so_far=_learned(deps))\n        )\n    except asyncio.TimeoutError:\n        return done(\n            BudgetExceeded(\n                limit=\"seconds\",\n                detail=f\"exceeded {settings.LOOP_MAX_SECONDS}s wall clock for the whole call\",\n                learned_so_far=_learned(deps),\n            )\n        )\n\n\ndef _check_spend(run: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Trip the spend budget BETWEEN steps (closes O-7).\n\n    Between steps is the only place it can be enforced: the cost of a request is\n    only knowable once its response has arrived, so the budget stops the *next*\n    request rather than the one that crossed the line. `LOOP_MAX_USD` is\n    therefore a ceiling on what a run may commit to spending, not a hard cap on\n    what it has spent — size it accordingly.\n    \"\"\"\n    spent, complete = usage.spend_usd(run.all_messages())\n    if spent > settings.LOOP_MAX_USD:\n        logger.warning(\n            \"spend budget exceeded\",\n            extra={\n                \"subsystem\": \"api\",\n                \"spent_usd\": spent,\n                \"limit_usd\": settings.LOOP_MAX_USD,\n                \"cost_complete\": complete,\n            },\n        )\n        raise SpendExceeded(spent, complete)\n\n\ndef _finish(\n    output: HarnessOutput,\n    runs: list[Any],\n    question: str,\n    started_at: datetime,\n    record_usage: bool,\n    deps: Deps,\n) -> HarnessOutput:\n    \"\"\"Hand the message history back to the caller, write the usage records, and\n    return the outcome unchanged.\n\n    The history goes onto `deps` on EVERY branch, including a budget trip: a\n    caller that wants to answer a clarification needs it, and a caller\n    inspecting a failed run needs it more. Telemetry never alters or fails a\n    result — `record_run` swallows its own errors (ADR-005). `runs` is empty\n    only when the agent never started (pipeline mode uses no agent).\n    \"\"\"\n    if runs:\n        deps.last_messages = list(runs[-1].all_messages())\n        if record_usage:\n            usage.record_run(\n                runs[-1],\n                question=question,\n                output_branch=type(output).__name__,\n                started_at=started_at,\n            )\n    return output\n\n\ndef _learned(deps: Deps) -> str:\n    \"\"\"What a budget breach can still tell the caller. Never a partial answer —\n    a half-rendered figure is worse than none.\"\"\"\n    parts = []\n    if deps.resolved_school_ids:\n        parts.append(f\"resolved school IDs {deps.resolved_school_ids}\")\n    if deps.last_envelope is not None:\n        parts.append(f\"fetched evidence for {deps.last_envelope['question_id']}\")\n    if deps.repair_attempts:\n        parts.append(f\"{deps.repair_attempts} request repair attempt(s)\")\n    return \"; \".join(parts)\n\n\ndef build_deps(client: EvidenceClient | None = None) -> Deps:\n    return Deps(client=client or EvidenceClient.from_settings())\n","numLines":630,"startLine":1,"totalLines":630}}}
