{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q4Zz7kqw8P1YEnNhpffeyA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"M4 — the live tier's machinery, exercised offline.\n2\t\n3\tThe live tier spends real tokens, so it runs manually and never gates a PR. But\n4\tits *arithmetic* must not wait for a paid run to be checked: a reporting bug in\n5\t`pass@k` / `pass^k` would misreport every live result afterwards, and the number\n6\tthat gets misreported is always the flattering one.\n7\t\n8\tSo everything here runs the real runner — `run_trial`, `run_suite`, the\n9\tsummariser, the report writer — with the model scripted. What is NOT proved here\n10\tis the only thing the live tier exists to measure: whether a real model makes\n11\tthe right decisions. That gap is the point of the tier, not an omission.\n12\t\n13\tThe paid tier itself is `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`, marked `live` and\n14\texcluded by `pytest.ini`.\n15\t\"\"\"\n16\t\n17\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n18\t\n19\timport ast\n20\timport asyncio\n21\timport json\n22\timport subprocess\n23\timport sys\n24\tfrom pathlib import Path\n25\t\n26\timport pytest\n27\tfrom pydantic_ai.messages import ModelMessage, ModelResponse, ToolCallPart\n28\tfrom pydantic_ai.models.function import AgentInfo, FunctionModel\n29\t\n30\tfrom evals import live, replay as replay_mod\n31\tfrom evals.live import CaseReport, TrialResult, aggregate, summarise\n32\tfrom evals.schema import load_cases, load_reference_solutions\n33\tfrom harness.agent import build_agent\n34\tfrom harness.intent import StructuredIntent\n35\t\n36\tPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n37\t\n38\tCASES = {c.case_id: c for c in load_cases()}\n39\tREFERENCES = load_reference_solutions()\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e8b7dde-8bb0-4345-aaad-7bcee95758ae","uuid":"062946c8-f54f-48f9-ad5a-237af7069df1","timestamp":"2026-09-26T10:09:13.634Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/tests/unit/test_live_tier.py","content":"\"\"\"M4 — the live tier's machinery, exercised offline.\n\nThe live tier spends real tokens, so it runs manually and never gates a PR. But\nits *arithmetic* must not wait for a paid run to be checked: a reporting bug in\n`pass@k` / `pass^k` would misreport every live result afterwards, and the number\nthat gets misreported is always the flattering one.\n\nSo everything here runs the real runner — `run_trial`, `run_suite`, the\nsummariser, the report writer — with the model scripted. What is NOT proved here\nis the only thing the live tier exists to measure: whether a real model makes\nthe right decisions. That gap is the point of the tier, not an omission.\n\nThe paid tier itself is `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`, marked `live` and\nexcluded by `pytest.ini`.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ast\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\nfrom pydantic_ai.messages import ModelMessage, ModelResponse, ToolCallPart\nfrom pydantic_ai.models.function import AgentInfo, FunctionModel\n\nfrom evals import live, replay as replay_mod\nfrom evals.live import CaseReport, TrialResult, aggregate, summarise\nfrom evals.schema import load_cases, load_reference_solutions\nfrom harness.agent import build_agent\nfrom harness.intent import StructuredIntent\n\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n\nCASES = {c.case_id: c for c in load_cases()}\nREFERENCES = load_reference_solutions()\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1011}}}
